WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.540
As an official, Hai Rui was honest and upright, lived a simple life, and everyone praised him for daring to speak the truth.

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:10.000
His clothes were patched, and on his dining table there were only simple greens and tofu.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:16.200
The Jiajing Emperor was already old; for a long time he did not attend court and only believed in magical arts.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:21.060
Incense smoke curled through the palace, while the ministers waited outside the door day after day.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:26.300
At night, Hai Rui wrote a memorial by candlelight, criticizing the emperor for neglecting state affairs.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:30.680
The candlelight flickered as he wrote very earnestly, stroke by stroke.

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:35.720
Holding the memorial in both hands, he walked into the palace, his expression firm and completely unafraid.

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:39.620
The great hall fell completely silent, and everyone held their breath.

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:44.520
Because of this, Hai Rui was arrested and imprisoned, yet he still kept his back straight and refused to bow his head.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:48.360
The guards looked at his upright figure from behind and felt deep admiration in their hearts.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:52.520
The story of how he risked his life to remonstrate made him a famous symbol of the honest official.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:58.580
The young officials quietly made up their minds to be upright, just like Hai Rui.
